## Building & Verifying

### Environment Prerequisites
- Python 3.11+
- PostgreSQL running locally on port 5432 with database `wiki`
- Google Cloud credentials configured (`gcloud auth application-default login`)

### Automated Verification Harness
Run the full 9-layer verification harness to validate directory structure, permissions, JSON schemas, domain contracts, wiki sync, Cadence CLI, and test suites:

```bash
python3 scripts/verify_bootstrap.py --verbose
```

Flags available:
- `--skip-network`: Skips live Firestore calls.
- `--skip-db`: Skips PostgreSQL connection checks.
- `--quick`: Runs fast local checks only.

### Running Unit Tests
```bash
python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -p "test_*.py"
```

### Checking & Stamping Drift
```bash
# Check all domains for drift (exits 1 if drift detected)
python3 scripts/drift_enforcer.py

# Stamp current git commit hashes into registries (run only during session-wrapup)
python3 scripts/drift_enforcer.py --stamp
```

